# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# prefs: factory
# The message window: what a run SAID, as rows, and a row that was
# about somewhere is a way to get there.
#
# The program is run on the interpreter a board runs -- the kernel's
# own engine, as a child on the far end of a pipe -- and what it says
# comes back as three things and no more: words, the file they were
# about, and the line.  That is the whole contract a build backend has
# to meet, and it is met here before any C exists.
wait 25
click 980 30
wait 4
menu-pick Applications
wait 4
menu-pick IDE
wait 150
expect-title Project
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Open Project…
wait 40
expect-title TikuTracker: Open
click 400 248
wait 6
click 675 413
wait 60
expect-no-title TikuTracker: Open
note the row the list is standing on is the one Run offers, and it is
note offered because its NAME says the interpreter would know it
click-window Project
wait 8
key Down
wait 8
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Run blink.bas
menu-pick Run blink.bas
wait 150
note the messages arrive in a window of their own, which was not there
note until there was something to put in it
expect-title Messages
note what the program said is a row, and it is about nowhere: there is
note nothing to go to, and the window says so rather than pretending
key Down
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu This one is not about anywhere
menu-pick This one is not about anywhere
wait 8
note the error is ONE row -- what happened and where, together -- and
note the place it names is offered
click-window Messages
wait 8
key Down
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
expect-menu Go to line 250
menu-pick Go to line 250
wait 90
note following it opened the file the message was about
expect-title blink.bas
note and put the caret ON that line, which the file itself can show:
note a letter typed here lands at the head of the line the run blamed,
note which is well past what the window was showing
key x shift
wait 10
click 71 8
wait 8
menu-pick Save blink.bas
wait 60
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/blink.bas X250 PRUNT
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/blink.bas X10 PRINT
